Both hand-derivation steps confirmed exact.

======================================================================
(1) FINAL closed form, end-to-end numeric verification (mpmath dps=50)
    T(n,m) =?= C(n+m+1,2m+1) * (2m+1)!/(m!)^2 *
               Integral_0^1 t^m (1-t)^m (1-g t)^(n-m) dt
======================================================================
Checked 40 (n,m,gamma) triples.
Max relative error: 4.418068194e-51

CONFIRMED to full quadrature precision (<1e-45 relative error):

  T(n,m) = C(n+m+1, 2m+1) * E_{t~Beta(m+1,m+1)}[ (1-gamma*t)^(n-m) ]

This is a genuine, previously-unwritten (by the target) usable
closed-form integral representation. The integrand t^m(1-t)^m is
(up to normalization) EXACTLY the Beta(m+1,m+1) density -- the
CONTINUUM analogue of the median order-statistic distribution the
target independently found in Sec.3! This ties the target's Sec.2
(2F1) and Sec.3 (order statistic) findings into a single coherent
object via the Pfaff-type fix they named but did not execute --
substantiating that it is a genuinely promising, not a red-herring,
next step, and handing a future front a clean, classical Beta-type
integral (ready for Watson's-lemma/Laplace analysis) in place of
raw Pochhammer-sum manipulation. This does NOT by itself close
C(gamma) -- the coupled outer m-sum Laplace analysis (target's own
Sec.5) is still required -- but it is a concrete, verified partial
advance beyond what the target itself reached on this specific
named-but-unexecuted next step.
